Fredholm theory: About fredholm integral equations. Which are the inverse of a differential equation.

Spectral theory diagonalizes operators. Writes complicated operators as sums of multiplicate operators.
Multiplicative operators are a generalization of diagonal matrices. Every element is just multiplied.

Fourier transformation is the spectral theory (diagonalization) of differential operators.

Normaled operators can also be diagonalized.
Examples of normal operators include:
- Unitary operators
- Hermitian (self-adjoint) operators

Every linear operator is a integral operator, if the kernel is allowed to be a distribution.

Important Theorems:
- Riesz Representation Theorem
- Spectral Theorem
